---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ObservatoryNav from '@components/observatory/ObservatoryNav.astro';
import { roleLabels, taxonomySource } from '@lib/taxonomy';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="How we calculate Observatory metrics and derive ecosystem status."
>
  <ObservatoryNav current="methodology" />
  <div class="methodology-page">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="page-intro page-header">
        <a href="/observatory" class="back-link">
          ← Observatory
        </a>
        <h1>Methodology</h1>
        <p>How we calculate Observatory metrics and derive ecosystem status</p>
      </header>

      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Data Sources</h2>
        <p>
          All data displayed in the Observatory is derived from the public
          <a href="https://data.directory.openfinance.ae" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            UAE Open Finance Trust Framework Directory
          </a>
          , operated by Raidiam on behalf of Nebras Open Finance LLC (a CBUAE subsidiary).
        </p>

        <div class="environment-info">
          <h3>Dual Environment Collection</h3>
          <p>We collect data from both environments of the UAE Open Finance Trust Framework:</p>
          <div class="env-grid">
            <div class="env-card production">
              <div class="env-header">
                <span class="env-dot"></span>
                <strong>Production</strong>
              </div>
              <p>
                The production directory publishes registrations, role claims and
                authorization-server metadata. Registration does not establish use of a service.
              </p>
              <code>data.directory.openfinance.ae</code>
            </div>
            <div class="env-card sandbox">
              <div class="env-header">
                <span class="env-dot"></span>
                <strong>Sandbox</strong>
              </div>
              <p>
                The sandbox directory publishes testing-environment registrations and metadata.
                Registration alone does not show testing activity or certification.
              </p>
              <code>data.sandbox.directory.openfinance.ae</code>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Observation Limits</h2>
        <p>
          The collector schema changed to version 2.1 on 8 October 2026 to preserve insurance, ATM
          and unknown API families. Older snapshots retain their original coverage; newly observed
          families can reflect this collection correction rather than a new deployment. Capability
          flags are source declarations, and an unmarked flag has not been tested. The Watch uses
          separate traffic logs with explicit reporting periods.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Update Frequency</h2>
        <p>
          Data is collected automatically once per day at <strong>06:00 UTC</strong> via a GitHub
          Actions workflow. Each collection creates timestamped snapshots for both production and
          sandbox environments.
        </p>
        <p>
          Historical snapshots are preserved, enabling trend analysis and visualization of ecosystem
          growth over time. Milestones (such as new participant registrations) are automatically
          tracked.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Metric Definitions</h2>

        <div class="metric-category">
          <h3>Core Metrics</h3>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Registrations</h4>
            <p>
              Count of distinct OrganisationId values after excluded test/support and unresolved
              unnamed records are filtered out. One legal entity may have multiple registrations.
              Cross-environment totals deduplicate IDs, not legal entities.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Authorization Server Published</h4>
            <p>
              Registrations with at least one active authorization server and a nonempty issuer
              field. We do not validate issuer reachability, certification, successful integration,
              or traffic. The JSON fields isLive and liveInProduction retain this meaning for
              compatibility.
            </p>
            <p>
              In the UAE, the API Hub is the OIDC/FAPI authorization server and token issuer.
              Metadata published under an LFI registration can describe that Hub endpoint; it does
              not establish that the institution issues TPP access tokens.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Directory Shariah Flag</h4>
            <p>
              Registrations whose source shariah_compliant flag includes True. This source
              declaration is not a classification of every Islamic finance institution, and
              editorial profiles are not used to overwrite it.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Multi-Role Participants</h4>
            <p>
              Registrations with two or more active role claims. This does not measure integration
              depth, usage, or licence category.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="metric-category">
          <h3>Participant Roles</h3>
          <p>
            Directory roles and permissions use the{' '}
            <a href={taxonomySource.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Trust Framework role documentation
            </a>{' '}
            (terminology reviewed {taxonomySource.version}). A role claim is separate from a licence
            or editorial company-type classification.
          </p>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>LFI — {roleLabels.LFI}</h4>
            <p>
              Regulated financial institutions, including banks and insurers, providing data or
              services through the central API Hub.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>BDSP — {roleLabels.BDSP}</h4>
            <p>
              Entities that provide data sharing services, enabling secure access to customer
              financial data.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>BSIP — {roleLabels.BSIP}</h4>
            <p>
              The directory role for bank service initiation. Consult the operator for the
              permissions attached to this claim.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>ISP — {roleLabels.ISP}</h4>
            <p>The directory role for insurance service provision.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>TPP — {roleLabels.TPP}</h4>
            <p>
              Fintech companies and other third parties that access Open Finance APIs to provide
              innovative financial services.
            </p>
          </div>

          <p class="note">
            A registration may hold multiple roles. TPP population is unavailable from these claims;
            the legacy tppCount field only counts explicit TPP claims.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="metric-category">
          <h3>API Families</h3>
          <p>
            Insurance and ATM families are preserved alongside banking families. Unknown family
            identifiers are retained verbatim, and every declared version and completeness flag is
            available in the dataset and participant detail. Absence from a snapshot is not proof
            that a service is unavailable.
          </p>
          <p>
            Derived from the API resources registered under each participant's authorization
            servers:
          </p>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Account Information</h4>
            <p>
              APIs for accessing account balances, transactions, and account holder information.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Payments</h4>
            <p>
              Payment Initiation APIs enabling authorized third parties to initiate payments on
              behalf of customers.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Confirmation of Payee (CoP)</h4>
            <p>
              APIs for verifying payee details before payment execution, reducing fraud and
              misdirected payments.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Products</h4>
            <p>
              Product Information APIs providing details about financial products offered by
              institutions.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="metric-category">
          <h3>Declared Authorization Capabilities</h3>
          <p>
            Flags declared on active authorization servers. Unmarked capabilities are not declared
            true; their availability has not been tested.
          </p>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>CIBA — Client Initiated Backchannel Authentication</h4>
            <p>
              Decoupled authentication flow where the authorization is initiated from a consumption
              device but authentication happens on a different device (e.g., mobile phone). Enhances
              security for headless and IoT scenarios.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>DCR — Dynamic Client Registration</h4>
            <p>
              Capability allowing Third Party Providers to register their applications dynamically
              via API, streamlining the onboarding process for TPPs.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Redirect Flow</h4>
            <p>
              The TPP initiates authorization through the API Hub. In the LFI redirect journey, the
              customer authenticates with the institution. The Hub owns the consent state and issues
              the access token. A declared redirect flag does not verify this journey.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="metric-category">
          <h3>Cross-Environment Analysis</h3>
          <p>When viewing "Both" environments, additional metrics are available:</p>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>In Both Environments</h4>
            <p>
              Registration IDs observed in both production and sandbox. Presence in both does not
              establish certification or successful integration.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Sandbox Only</h4>
            <p>
              Registration IDs observed in sandbox and absent from the production snapshot. This
              does not establish a testing phase, certification status or planned launch.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="metric-definition">
            <h4>Production Only</h4>
            <p>
              Registration IDs observed in production and absent from the sandbox snapshot. This
              does not establish a graduation event or previous sandbox participation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Historical Trends</h2>
        <p>
          The Observatory tracks ecosystem growth over time by preserving daily snapshots. The
          Ecosystem Growth chart displays:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Total participant count over time</li>
          <li>Net change in participants (growth/decline)</li>
          <li>Milestones marking when new participants joined</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Historical data is automatically aggregated from daily snapshots to provide trend
          visualization without requiring manual data entry.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Known Limitations</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            We only display publicly available metadata; we cannot verify actual API functionality
            or performance
          </li>
          <li>
            Participant counts may differ from official CBUAE statistics due to registration timing
            differences
          </li>
          <li>
            TPP population cannot be inferred from role claims. The legacy explicit-claim count does
            not indicate how many licensed TPPs exist.
          </li>
          <li>Historical data before the launch of this Observatory is not available</li>
          <li>
            Sandbox data availability depends on the public API being accessible (may require
            authentication in future)
          </li>
          <li>
            Authorization capability flags (CIBA, DCR, Redirect) reflect declared support, not
            verified functionality
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Data Freshness</h2>
        <p>
          The "Last updated" timestamp shown on the Observatory indicates when the data was last
          collected. If collection fails (e.g., API unavailable), the previous snapshot is retained
          and the timestamp reflects the last successful collection.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each environment (production and sandbox) is collected independently. If one environment
          fails, the other may still be updated successfully.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Open Source</h2>
        <p>
          The collector script and all data transformations are open source. You can review the code
          at:
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/openfinance-os" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            github.com/openfinance-os
          </a>
        </p>
        <p>Key files:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>scripts/collect-observatory.ts</code> — Data collection and transformation
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>scripts/utils/directory-client.ts</code> — API client for both environments
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>scripts/types/participant.ts</code> — TypeScript type definitions
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>data/observatory/</code> — Snapshots and historical data
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you find an error or have suggestions, please
          <a
            href="https://github.com/openfinance-os/community-website/issues"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            open an issue
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .methodology-page {
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4) var(--space-16);
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-brand-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .page-header p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .content-section p {
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .content-section ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .content-section li {
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .content-section a {
    color: var(--color-brand-ink);
  }

  .content-section code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    background: var(--color-soft);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .environment-info {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  .environment-info h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .env-grid {
    min-width: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  @media (min-width: 500px) {
    .env-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .env-card {
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid;
  }

  .env-card.production {
    background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.05);
    border-color: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.2);
  }

  .env-card.sandbox {
    background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.05);
    border-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.2);
  }

  .env-header {
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .env-dot {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .env-card.production .env-dot {
    background: var(--color-success);
  }

  .env-card.sandbox .env-dot {
    background: var(--color-warning);
  }

  .env-card p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .env-card code {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .metric-category {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .metric-category h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .metric-category > p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .metric-definition {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .metric-definition h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .metric-definition p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .metric-definition p:last-child,
  .metric-definition ul:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .metric-definition ul {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .note {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
